        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Sulphuric acid is soluble in water and hygroscopic in nature. It readily absorbs water vapour from the air. Anhydrous H₂SO₄ is a very polar liquid. It is highly corrosive to various materials. On contacting the skin, it causes chemical burns. Some physical properties of sulphuric acid are given in Table 12.4.",
